 {"id":"fabro-e4c4","title":"Develop evidence node: deliver the capture inline via output_schema","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T15:14:48.322Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T15:24:21.820Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro, give the evidence node an output_schema (e.g. @schemas/evidence-capture.schema.json) and declare it in context_allow_keys, mirroring how gatebounce ships stdout inline as output.gate_known_bug_hits; swap the reviewer's preamble_allow_keys entry from command.output to output.evidence. In run 01M20RK7XFNPJRZ2T437XGDEP8 the 12.4 KB capture reached the reviewer as a blob ref with a ~300-byte preview, forcing a read_file detour plus one extra model round inside its 42.0s inference (the reviewer's own journal painpoint). Expected effect: one tool call and one model round removed per review, and the verification_blocked-on-blob failure mode disappears; composes with open seeds fabro-9ef9 (evidence re-key, overwrite fix) and fabro-c1bb (drop duplicated brief spec) rather than duplicating them — 12.4 KB fits the 16 KB inline ceiling once the duplicated spec is dropped. Basis: run 01M20RK7XFNPJRZ2T437XGDEP8, workflow version af036506627c2c235dc58d52e1ceda475fc4053f219b513e9582f644224dc129, commit 6f23b48525bf1ff7b11d3a4c49ad43681a9ff1fb","labels":["revision","workflows"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-a08a","title":"Develop planner prompt: visit-1 fresh-cycle line to skip dead context reads","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T15:14:55.468Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T15:24:21.706Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 1, add one line: 'visit 1 with no current_seed_id in ## Context = fresh cycle; go straight to sd ready'. In run 01M20RK7XFNPJRZ2T437XGDEP8 the planner opened with two context_read calls at pass start, one erroring with unknown context key 'current_seed_id' because it was visit 1 and nothing existed to read (events seq 31-34). Expected effect: two fewer tool rounds per fresh planner pass (~$0.02, ~8 s of the 59.7 s stage); orthogonal to fabro-c3b4 (top-N view, output volume) and fabro-e4fa (call economy). Basis: run 01M20RK7XFNPJRZ2T437XGDEP8, workflow version af036506627c2c235dc58d52e1ceda475fc4053f219b513e9582f644224dc129, commit 6f23b48525bf1ff7b11d3a4c49ad43681a9ff1fb","labels":["revision","workflows"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-fc1b","title":"Implementer prompt: require the full touched-crate test suite when the seed touches tests","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T16:34:54.153Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T18:11:08.818Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 4, replace the 'ONE focused test' verification rule with: when the seed adds or edits tests in a crate, the pre-gate check is cargo nextest -p <touched-crate> (full crate suite), still never the workspace suite. Evidence from run 01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP: implementer@1 ran targeted fabro-server tests only and missed the two pre-existing Docker-socket failures (run_start_grants_github_token_bridge_only_to_user_principals, worker_principal_run_without_vault_token_takes_no_token_path) that live in the full fabro-server suite; the resulting gate-red bounce (tester@1 340s + implementer@2 915s/$0.769 + tester@2 91s) cost ~22 min, ~40% of the 55-min run wall, to apply a 6-line [run.environment] id = \"local\" pin. Expected effect: pre-existing or adjacent breaks in the touched crate surface in the same implementer pass, eliminating ~20 min / ~$0.8 per bounce of this class. Distinct from closed seeds fabro-0d56/fabro-2254 (fmt/clippy scope) which cover lint checks, not the test-suite scope. Basis: run 01M20T9S8JRXETASN64768TRRP, workflow version 8aedc5a9bbdd71b2f882af0b6c7d28a947212553646a31a390f5d173a91c8a69, commit 9966d125e665593fcd4f21137a19659625d58ed0","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-8d1c","title":"ADR-0019: record the engine-provided-credentials doctrine in the ADR file itself (PR #68 landed prompts-only)","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T18:11:58.469Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T20:02:35.955Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"ADR-0019 doctrine extension (PR #68: 'treat engine-provided credentials as agent-reachable capabilities') landed ONLY in workflow prompts (.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md step 5, .fabro/workflows/revisor/prompts/file.md capability paragraph) - the ADR file itself (docs/lab/adr/0019-capability-gate-for-agent-surfaces.md) does not mention engine-provided credentials at all: no reference to the GITHUB_TOKEN injection via resolve_workflow_env (lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/services.rs), the git credential bridge (lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/git_bridge.rs), or the rule that a diff merely USING an engine-provided credential on a new code path is a capability delta requiring recorded user approval.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: the ADR is the durable decision record; prompts get rewritten by every revision pass and are agent-reachable surface themselves. Reviewers, revisors, and future grill sessions cite ADR-0019 - if the record omits the engine-provided-credential class, the gate doctrine silently narrows back to container-env-visible capability on the next prompt rewrite (exactly the PR #53 blind spot the extension closed).\n\nFIX: add one paragraph to ADR-0019 Decision section (or a numbered extension like .7) stating: engine-provided credentials and bridges (GITHUB_TOKEN injection, git credential bridge) ARE agent-reachable capability; diffs that use them on new code paths are capability deltas requiring recorded user approval; cite PR #68, run 01M20RK7XFNPJRZ2T437XGDEP8, and the fabro-16ff user directive (2026-09-08). Docs-only change, no code.\n\nBasis: agent sweep of other-machine runs 2026-09-08 evening, commit e078c27b2 (PR #68) vs docs/lab/adr/0019-capability-gate-for-agent-surfaces.md, commit 47b491b8e (repo state).","labels":["revision"]}
